   "subject": "cell size and geom_tile",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear list members,<p>I am trying to replicate a spatial plot (sample1.pdf) with Lat, Lon and <br>corresponding values in ggplot2 using geom_tile. However, the size of <br>cells is different. How i can adjust the size of the cells, to make it <br>look like the plot in sample.pdf.<p>Here the code i used:<p>dum = read.csv(&#39;1.csv&#39;, header = TRUE, sep=&#39;,&#39;)<br>dum$Lat&lt;-round(dum$Lat, digits=2)<br>dum$Lon&lt;-round(dum$Lon, digits=2)<br>dum$Value&lt;-round(dum$Value, digits=2)<p>ggplot(dum, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))<p>In case if you cannot see my attachment: here s a sample :)<p>Lat&lt;-c(50.75680902, 50.86917489, 50.86917489, 50.98153859, 50.98153859, <br>51.09390011, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.31861664, <br>51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, <br>51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, <br>51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, <br>51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165)<br>Lat&lt;-round(Lat, digits=2)<p>Lon&lt;-c(6.001151821, 5.737677201, 5.915246683, 5.829642345, 6.007640087, <br>5.92276702, 5.659333881, 5.838196438, 6.017058995, 3.423038765, <br>3.602337923, 3.781637081, 3.960936239, 4.140235397, 5.216030346, <br>5.395329504, 5.574628662, 5.75392782, 5.933226978, 6.112526137, <br>3.872574776, 4.052313363, 4.23205195, 4.591529125, 4.951006299, <br>5.130744886, 5.310483474, 5.490222061, 5.669960648)<br>Lon&lt;-round(Lon, digits=2)<p>Value&lt;-c(51.5531616, 52.4165268, 51.9916573, 53.2101517, 53.0154381, <br>54.6226883, 55.1447945, 54.9156456, 55.8886223, 49.2638474, 47.0254936, <br>50.5006256, 52.2497025, 55.4737206, 56.1528969, 56.2830505, 55.8317413, <br>55.1550751, 55.7404175, 58.8827209, 43.2671585, 46.7214737, 47.4093056, <br>48.0084763, 51.759243, 53.8048401, 54.1792603, 54.9313469, 54.7651978)<br>Value&lt;-round(Value, digits=2)<p>df&lt;-data.frame(Lon=Lon, Lat=Lat, Value=Value)<br>ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))<p>Thanks a lot for the help.<p>Cheers,<br>Navin<br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
