     1,
     "Hi Navin,<p></p>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<p>On Wed, Aug 24, 2011 at 12:07 PM, Swagath Navin &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">swagat...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br>&gt; Dear list members,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; I am trying to replicate a spatial plot (sample1.pdf) with Lat, Lon and<br>&gt; corresponding values in ggplot2 using geom_tile. However, the size of cells<br>&gt; is different. How i can adjust the size of the cells, to make it look like<br>&gt; the plot in sample.pdf.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Here the code i used:<br>&gt;<br>&gt; dum = read.csv(&#39;1.csv&#39;, header = TRUE, sep=&#39;,&#39;)<br>&gt; dum$Lat&lt;-round(dum$Lat, digits=2)<br>&gt; dum$Lon&lt;-round(dum$Lon, digits=2)<br>&gt; dum$Value&lt;-round(dum$Value, digits=2)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; ggplot(dum, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))<br>&gt;<br>&gt; In case if you cannot see my attachment: here s a sample :)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Lat&lt;-c(50.75680902, 50.86917489, 50.86917489, 50.98153859, 50.98153859,<br>&gt; 51.09390011, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.31861664,<br>&gt; 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664,<br>&gt; 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664,<br>&gt; 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165,<br>&gt; 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165)<br>&gt; Lat&lt;-round(Lat, digits=2)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Lon&lt;-c(6.001151821, 5.737677201, 5.915246683, 5.829642345, 6.007640087,<br>&gt; 5.92276702, 5.659333881, 5.838196438, 6.017058995, 3.423038765, 3.602337923,<br>&gt; 3.781637081, 3.960936239, 4.140235397, 5.216030346, 5.395329504,<br>&gt; 5.574628662, 5.75392782, 5.933226978, 6.112526137, 3.872574776, 4.052313363,<br>&gt; 4.23205195, 4.591529125, 4.951006299, 5.130744886, 5.310483474, 5.490222061,<br>&gt; 5.669960648)<br>&gt; Lon&lt;-round(Lon, digits=2)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Value&lt;-c(51.5531616, 52.4165268, 51.9916573, 53.2101517, 53.0154381,<br>&gt; 54.6226883, 55.1447945, 54.9156456, 55.8886223, 49.2638474, 47.0254936,<br>&gt; 50.5006256, 52.2497025, 55.4737206, 56.1528969, 56.2830505, 55.8317413,<br>&gt; 55.1550751, 55.7404175, 58.8827209, 43.2671585, 46.7214737, 47.4093056,<br>&gt; 48.0084763, 51.759243, 53.8048401, 54.1792603, 54.9313469, 54.7651978)<br>&gt; Value&lt;-round(Value, digits=2)<br>&gt;<br>&gt; df&lt;-data.frame(Lon=Lon, Lat=Lat, Value=Value)<br>&gt; ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))</p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p><p>geom_tile accepts a (mostly undocumented: appears only in the<br>examples) width aesthetic, so you can do e.g.,<p>ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value, width = .2))<p>If you want to get more complicated you could do something like<p>df &lt;- df[order(df$Lon),]<br>df &lt;- ddply(df, .(Lat), transform,<br>            lon.w = c(0, diff(Lon)))<p>ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value, width = lon.w))<p>but I haven&#39;t worked out how to deal with the fact that there is one<br>less value than there is width.<p>Best,<br>Ista<p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p>&gt;<br>&gt; Thanks a lot for the help.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Cheers,<br>&gt; Navin<br>&gt;<br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p><p>&gt; --<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing<br>&gt; list.<br>&gt; Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378648889000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2QHupvX-JJm_jfXfflxnwU\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a><br>&gt;<br>&gt; To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>&gt; More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378648889000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2fw763e8fI2O_6rL0CKWz4\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br>&gt;<p><p>-- <br>Ista Zahn<br>Graduate student<br>University of Rochester<br>Department of Clinical and Social Psychology<br><a href=\"http://yourpsyche.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://yourpsyche.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378648889000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3dZzjQc3TC8z-WQxWZuScn\">http://yourpsyche.org</a><br></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p></p>"
