  {
   "id": "42H6M8WjOj8J",
   "from": "David Kahle",
   "author": "e4aec126ff1dca22",
   "date": "2011-08-24T17:35:12Z",
   "subject": "Re: cell size and geom_tile",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div>Hi Swagath -<br><br>Something like this should do the trick....<br><br>df &lt;- read.csv(file.choose())<br><br>ggplot(aes(x = Lon, y = Lat, fill = Value), data = df) +<br> geom_point() # so the points are there...<br><br>ggplot(aes(x = Lon, y = Lat, fill = Value), data = df) +<br> geom_tile() # the bad plot you&#39;re getting<br><br># make latitude maxes (uniform, so easy)<br>diff(sort(df$Lat))<br>df &lt;- transform(df, latmax = Lat + resolution(Lat))<br><br># make latitude maxes (nonuniform, so a little more complicated)<br>diff(sort(df$Lon))<br>qplot(diff(sort(Lon)), data = df, geom = &#39;density&#39;)<br>df &lt;- ddply(df, .(Lat), function(df){<br> transform(df, lonmax = Lon + min(resolution(Lon), .2))<br>})<br><br># plot<br>ggplot(aes(fill = Value), data = df) +<br> geom_rect(aes(xmin = Lon, xmax = lonmax, ymin = Lat, ymax = latmax))<br><br><br>Cheers<br>david.</div><div><br></div><br><div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div>On Aug 24, 2011, at 11:07 AM, Swagath Navin wrote:</div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>Dear list members,<br><br>I am trying to replicate a spatial plot (sample1.pdf) with Lat, Lon and corresponding values in ggplot2 using geom_tile. However, the size of cells is different. How i can adjust the size of the cells, to make it look like the plot in sample.pdf.<br><br>Here the code i used:<br><br>dum = read.csv(&#39;1.csv&#39;, header = TRUE, sep=&#39;,&#39;)<br>dum$Lat&lt;-round(dum$Lat, digits=2)<br>dum$Lon&lt;-round(dum$Lon, digits=2)<br>dum$Value&lt;-round(dum$Value, digits=2)<br><br>ggplot(dum, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))<br><br>In case if you cannot see my attachment: here s a sample :)<br><br>Lat&lt;-c(50.75680902, 50.86917489, 50.86917489, 50.98153859, 50.98153859, 51.09390011, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.20625946, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.31861664, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165, 51.43097165)<br>Lat&lt;-round(Lat, digits=2)<br><br>Lon&lt;-c(6.001151821, 5.737677201, 5.915246683, 5.829642345, 6.007640087, 5.92276702, 5.659333881, 5.838196438, 6.017058995, 3.423038765, 3.602337923, 3.781637081, 3.960936239, 4.140235397, 5.216030346, 5.395329504, 5.574628662, 5.75392782, 5.933226978, 6.112526137, 3.872574776, 4.052313363, 4.23205195, 4.591529125, 4.951006299, 5.130744886, 5.310483474, 5.490222061, 5.669960648)<br>Lon&lt;-round(Lon, digits=2)<br><br>Value&lt;-c(51.5531616, 52.4165268, 51.9916573, 53.2101517, 53.0154381, 54.6226883, 55.1447945, 54.9156456, 55.8886223, 49.2638474, 47.0254936, 50.5006256, 52.2497025, 55.4737206, 56.1528969, 56.2830505, 55.8317413, 55.1550751, 55.7404175, 58.8827209, 43.2671585, 46.7214737, 47.4093056, 48.0084763, 51.759243, 53.8048401, 54.1792603, 54.9313469, 54.7651978)<br>Value&lt;-round(Value, digits=2)<br><br>df&lt;-data.frame(Lon=Lon, Lat=Lat, Value=Value)<br>ggplot(df, aes(x=Lon, y=Lat))+geom_tile(aes(fill=Value))<br><br>Thanks a lot for the help.<br><br>Cheers,<br>Navin<br><br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div>-- <br>You received this message because you are subscribed to the ggplot2 mailing list.<br>Please provide a reproducible example: <a href=\"http://gist.github.com/270442\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://gist.github.com/270442&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378648892000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0VZSyuctnCEzUcuCaCwpv5\">http://gist.github.com/270442</a><br><br>To post: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggp...@googlegroups.com</a><br>To unsubscribe: email <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">ggplot2+u...@googlegroups.com</a><br>More options: <a href=\"http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792378648892000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1STPiGjnRcv15dI9nlFK53\">http://groups.google.com/group/ggplot2</a><br></div></blockquote></div></div>"
